(This paper provides a comprehensive systematic review of autonomous multi-agent) Tj
T*
(systems operating in digital commerce. We formalize the transition from human-centric) Tj
T*
(graphical user interfaces to machine-to-machine agentic transactions. We establish) Tj
T*
('THE BAR' governance framework: requiring autonomous financial operations to be) Tj
T*
(Explainable, Bounded, Gated, Auditable, and Gracefully Recoverable. We analyze the) Tj
T*
(intersection of agentic procurement and instant settlement networks like Razorpay.) Tj
T*

/F1 11 Tf
T*
(1. Introduction and Problem Formulation) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
T*
(The emergence of large multimodal models [LMMs] has enabled autonomous software) Tj
T*
(agents to perform complex procurement tasks previously reserved for human operators.) Tj
T*
(However, deploying autonomous buyers into production commerce environments introduces) Tj
T*
(severe financial and operational risks: unauthorized discounting, hallucinations, and) Tj
T*
(catastrophic payment cascade failures. We propose a formal taxonomy of agentic) Tj
T*
(commerce capabilities.) Tj
T*

/F1 11 Tf
T*
(2. The BAR Governance Framework) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
T*
(We define the five cardinal pillars of safe agentic commerce: - Explainable: Every) Tj
T*
(parameter must have deterministic provenance. - Bounded: Financial actions must) Tj
T*
(operate strictly within clamped mathematical envelopes [P_min, P_max]. - Gated:) Tj
T*
(Tiered risk triggers mandatory multi-signature human approval. - Audit Trail:) Tj
T*
(Immutable SHA-256 state ledger linking every decision to source documents. - Graceful) Tj
T*
(Failure: Sub-200ms error containment with automated fallback links.) Tj
T*

